     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Friendly Davis-R Users/Soon-to-be-Users,<div><br></div><div>The Fall Quarter is upon us, and we are starting our weekly work-sessions this week. <i><b>Our meeting/worksessions this quarter will be Thursdays 10am -- 12pm, in 360 Shields Library (the <a href=\"http://dsi.ucdavis.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dsi.ucdavis.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466724491000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fAlHd16M-K3LaoINUSRU3\">DSI</a>).</b></i></div><div><b><i><br></i></b></div><div>Our work-sessions are open to any/all who have questions about using R, or who want some dedicated space to work for a few hours. Just learning? Come visit! We&#39;ll do our best to answer your questions. Plus you can always email the list-serv and generally get an answer. Check <a href=\"http://d-rug.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d-rug.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466724491000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QWyAXXawM8fmmjOOvG6Z-\">our website</a> for more resources</div><div><br></div><div>We have a few talks scheduled this quarter, thanks to speakers for volunteering their time. Tentatively the fall quarter schedule is as follows (all from 10-12). We&#39;ll try to webcast the talks as well, and recordings will be available on the website.</div><div><ul><li><b>Oct 26: Brandon Hurr</b> - &quot;Using purrr::map/map2/pmap and the walk family&quot;</li><li><b>Nov 2: Rich Pauloo</b> - &quot;R Markdown Basics: share code and visualizations online, create a CV, build a personal website, and more!&quot;</li><li><b>Nov 16: Kate Tiedeman</b> - &quot;Using R for geospatial research&quot;</li></ul><div>Thanks and look forward to seeing you all throughout the quarter.</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Adios,<br>Ryan</div><div><br></div><div>(D-RUG Coordinator)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline\"><span> </span></span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></b></i></font></span><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><font size=\"1\"><i>&quot;When we try to pick out anything by itself, we find it hitched to everything else in the universe.&quot;<b><br>John Muir (My First Summer in the Sierra, 1911)</b></i></font></div><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b>-----------------------------------------------------</b></i></font></span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;line-height:19px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><div>Ryan Peek</div><div>PhD Candidate, Graduate Group in Ecology<br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Center for Watershed Sciences, UC Davis</div></font></span><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><div><b style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;,serif\"><i><a href=\"http://ryanpeek.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ryanpeek.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466724491000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LDVKILEMMYXaY7h_lYOhP\">ryanpeek.github.io</a></i></b><br></div><div><b style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;,serif\">@riverpeek</b></div></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;,serif\"><span></span><a href=\"http:///\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http:///&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466724491000&amp;usg=AOvVaw103CTSvK8rrsSw3UHRDA97\"></a><span></span><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/IevI-V2nPkSsFIN18UQ--VXRc6BrR0Rxyt54_p8f-33BWibfVhrlRVsNtQJaWZIYUyS_y7N8DductXmF4ubkMxPr6f8PGj6p1eXBK0x4jtCB=s0-d-